# Meowcraft OHOS port — ref/lwjgl local patch 0001
#
# generator: write generated Java directly (bypass JDK 9+ JavacFiler)
#
# On JDK 9+ JavacFiler refuses to create a source file whose type name already
# exists among the compilation inputs. LWJGL2's *core* templates declare exactly
# the FQN they generate (templates/org/lwjgl/opengl/GL14.java declares
# org.lwjgl.opengl.GL14), so the generator aborted with:
#
#   java.lang.RuntimeException:
#   -- Failed to process template: org.lwjgl.opengl.GL14 --
#   Caused by: javax.annotation.processing.FilerException:
#     Attempt to recreate a file for type org.lwjgl.opengl.GL14
#
# Extension templates are unaffected because their declared name keeps the
# underscores while @Extension.className strips them, so the FQNs differ; GL14 is
# simply the first same-name template in the template iteration order.
#
# Upstream ran the generator on JDK 6/7, before that check existed. We drive the
# processor with `-proc:only` and compile the generated sources in a separate
# javac pass, so bypassing the Filer (writing the already-computed outputJava
# path directly) is safe.
#
# Apply from the ref/lwjgl checkout root:
#     git apply <this file>
#
